Another inning in which Joe Kernen throws softballs to a guest - in this case to Brad Gerstner @altcap
on @SquawkCNBC this morning. I am shocked (tongue in cheek)!  

Lazy Joe, let me do your homework for you and provide  real and more penetrating questions you can ask next time Brad appears on @CNBC 

But here are the rules of the game - you must demand specific and clear answers. (Brad, feel free to respond to me on twitter with the answers)  

Brad--  

* You said you wanted a $5 billion allocation on the ANT IP.  How much specifically did you end up putting in for, across all funds and break it down by fund. 
* How much did you specifically get, by fund?  
* If it was short of $5 billion, did you accumulate in the market to take your position up to $5 billion?  How much exactly did you buy?  If not enough to get up to $5 billion, why not, since you said you wanted $5 billion and this is a multi-year compounder.  
* Why would the price matter so much if a multi year compounder?  
* Are you saying it is overvalued if you didn’t buy where it was trading?  What is fair value then?  If fair value is higher, why are not you buying?  
* Did you sell any of your allocation?  Yes/No?  
* What exactly is your current position?  You don’t know?  How do you not know?  Why would someone want to invest with you as a limited partner if you apparently don’t know what you are buying and selling and what your current position is?
